      "workspace": "fixtures/repos/fix_impl_flag",
      "issue": "main.py: the --impl option (node=kind, which switches a node of the pipeline between 'fake' and 'llm') is not validated. A mistyped node such as --impl evalutor=llm is accepted and silently ignored, so the run goes on with the fake evaluator while the user believes the real one is used. An item without '=', with an empty node or kind, or with a kind other than exactly 'fake' or 'llm' (for example 'llmm' or 'LLM') fails late inside the graph with a traceback, after the run directory and its checkpoint were created, so the corrected command with the same --run-id is then refused as an existing run. Every invalid --impl must be refused before anything is created, the way --model already is: a 'config error: ...' message on stderr (no traceback) and exit code 1. For an unknown node the message names the node and lists the valid ones (orchestrator, worker, synthesize, evaluator); for a wrong kind it names the node, the value and the allowed ones ('fake' or 'llm'). Kinds are not normalised: 'LLM' is refused. Valid --impl flags, no flag, repeated --impl for one node (the last one wins) and --model behave exactly as before. Change only main.py and models/registry.py; the tests are protected."
    },
    "scope": {
      "writable": [
        "main.py",
        "models/registry.py"
      ],
      "protected": [
